WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:05.893
Their key idea is to view uncertainty
quantification through the lens of rate-distortion theory.

00:00:05.973 --> 00:00:11.306
They compress the entire training set into a small
codebook of prototype distributions,

00:00:11.386 --> 00:00:14.665
and measure how far a new input is from that codebook.

00:00:14.745 --> 00:00:17.216
This gives the Distance Aware Bottleneck,

00:00:17.296 --> 00:00:22.380
or DAB: a single deterministic model that produces
uncertainty in one forward pass.

00:00:22.460 --> 00:00:27.731
Along the way they contribute a practical
alternating-minimization training algorithm,

00:00:27.811 --> 00:00:32.646
a meta-probabilistic distortion that operates over
distributions of embeddings,

00:00:32.726 --> 00:00:38.370
and a post-hoc variant that adds distance awareness
to large pre-trained feature extractors.
